{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"4fecf7a81bb3da0b916af13822125f947ccb650ab47d71975f46bcbfe6aa5b7c","packTokens":4329,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":41,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spec","tokens":4268,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"State, as numbered plain sentences (n = 1, 2, ...), what change this spec asks for. Don't add anything the spec doesn't say. Don't mention IDs.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Feedlot API shall implement every HTTP operation, request and response schema, parameter, and documented status in contracts/openapi.yaml, retain its API documentation page, and omit product-facing screens.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given Operational data is available. when A client sends GET /overview. then The response status is 200 and the response fields include active lot and pen counts, total animals, pens, lot performance, inventory status, ration usage, bunk rates, planned and actual feed, feed quantities and cost, weights, gains, efficiency, energy, and best and worst lots.\",\n    \"Given Import batches are available. when A client sends GET /imports/batches. then The response status is 200 and the returned batches list contains records with batchId, sourceName, and recordCount fields.\",\n    \"Given A known import batch is available for preview. when A client sends POST /imports/preview with the contract request body. then The response status is 200 and the returned preview contains batchId, rows, readyCount, duplicateCount, pendingMappingCount, and failedCount fields.\",\n    \"Given A known import batch is available for synchronization. when A client sends POST /imports/synchronize with the contract request body. then The response status is 200 and the returned sync response contains the documented outcome counts, partial value, and row outcomes.\",\n    \"Given Lot and pen records are available. when A client sends GET /lots. then The response status is 200 and the returned lots and pens lists contain records matching the contract Lot and Pen schemas.\",\n    \"Given The source purchase-order line, lots, and pens in a mapping request exist. when A client sends POST /lots/mappings with valid assignments. then The response status is 200 and the returned assignments include the source line, requested head count, capacity, current animal count, status, and problem detail for each requested assignment.\",\n    \"Given The requested lot exists and the assumption values are valid. when A client sends PATCH /lots/{lotId}/assumptions with targetWeightLb and defaultGainRateLbPerDay. then The response status is 200 and the returned forecast contains the updated target weight and gain rate, gain-rate basis, projected market date, and recommendations.\",\n    \"Given The requested lot exists. when A client sends GET /lots/{lotId}/forecast. then The response status is 200 and the returned forecast contains targetWeightLb, gainRateLbPerDay, gainRateBasis, projectedMarketDate, and recommendations.\",\n    \"Given Feed inventory records exist. when A client sends GET /inventory/items. then The response status is 200 and the returned inventory response contains wastageRatio and item records with contract stock totals, item properties, and movement history.\",\n    \"Given The inventory item exists and a received or adjustment movement is valid. when A client sends POST /inventory/movements. then The response status is 201 and the returned movement and item reflect the submitted itemId, movementType, date, quantityLb, and note, including updated stock fields.\",\n    \"Given The inventory item exists and the actual-wastage request is valid. when A client sends POST /inventory/wastage. then The response status is 201 and the returned movement and item include the actual_wastage quantity, date, wastage cause, and updated stock fields.\",\n    \"Given The requested wastageRatio is valid. when A client sends PATCH /inventory/settings. then The response status is 200 and the returned wastageRatio value equals the saved submitted value.\",\n    \"Given Inventory data exists and a supported horizon and valid wastageRatio are supplied. when A client sends GET /inventory/outlook for each supported horizon: daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, bi-annual, and annual. then Each response status is 200 and each returned outlook contains the requested horizon, wastageRatio, and per-item current stock, daily estimated consumption, and projected balance fields.\",\n    \"Given Ration records exist or the ration list is empty. when A client sends GET /rations. then The response status is 200 and the returned rations list contains records with the contract ration and ingredient fields, including identity, type, target weight range, operational status, costPerLb, and ingredients.\",\n    \"Given Every ingredient item exists and the ration request is valid. when A client sends POST /rations. then The response status is 201 and the returned ration record includes its identity, type, target weight range, operational status, ingredients, and calculated costPerLb.\",\n    \"Given Inventory ingredients are available and the optimization constraints are valid. when A client sends POST /rations/optimize. then The response status is 200 and the returned feasibleCandidates and infeasibleCandidates contain feasibility, ingredient mix, costPerLb, predicted dry matter, and predicted energy fields in the contract cost order.\",\n    \"Given The requested candidateId exists and is available for selection. when A client sends POST /rations/selection. then The response status is 200 and the returned selectedCandidate matches the requested candidate and the applied field is false.\",\n    \"Given Feeding plans exist for the requested date and pen. when A client sends GET /feeding/plans with optional date and penId filters. then The response status is 200 and the returned plans list contains FeedingPlan records matching the filters and contract schema fields.\",\n    \"Given The requested pen and ration exist and the feeding-plan request is valid. when A client sends POST /feeding/plans. then The response status is 201 and the returned plan contains date, pen and lot details, animal count, ration, planned quantity and time, quantity per animal, total feed cost, expected energy, status, actual quantity, and variance fields.\",\n    \"Given Feeding activities exist for the requested date and pen. when A client sends GET /feeding/activities with optional date and penId filters. then The response status is 200 and the returned activities list contains FeedingActivity records matching the filters and contract schema fields.\",\n    \"Given The requested pen, ration, optional feeding plan, and lot quantities are valid and inventory is sufficient. when A client sends POST /feeding/activities. then The response status is 201 and the returned activity includes planned and actual quantities, variance, status, feed cost, energy, ingredient consumption, and lot consumption.\",\n    \"Given The requested lot exists and has weight readings. when A client sends GET /lots/{lotId}/weight-readings. then The response status is 200 and the returned readings list contains the lot's WeightReading fields in date order.\",\n    \"Given The requested lot exists and the weight-reading request is valid. when A client sends POST /lots/{lotId}/weight-readings. then The response status is 201 and the returned WeightMutationResponse contains the reading series and refreshed performance metrics.\",\n    \"Given The requested lot and reading exist and the replacement request is valid. when A client sends PUT /lots/{lotId}/weight-readings/{readingId}. then The response status is 200 and the returned WeightMutationResponse contains the updated reading series and refreshed performance metrics.\",\n    \"Given The requested lot and reading exist and deletion is permitted. when A client sends DELETE /lots/{lotId}/weight-readings/{readingId}. then The response status is 200 and the returned WeightMutationResponse contains the remaining reading series and refreshed performance metrics.\",\n    \"Given The requested lot exists and has controlled weight and feeding records. when A client sends GET /lots/{lotId}/performance. then The response status is 200 and the returned metrics contain daysOnFeed, totalWeightGainLb, averageDailyGainLbPerDay, totalFeedConsumedAsFedLb, feedConversionRatio, feedCostPerPoundOfGain, and projectedShipDate.\",\n    \"Given Operational records exist and startDate and endDate are valid. when A client sends GET /reports/operations with the required date range. then The response status is 200 and the returned report contains the requested dates and pens, lots, inventory, planAlignment, and rationUsage lists.\",\n    \"Given Weight and feeding records exist and the date range and optional breed, sex, and penId filters are valid. when A client sends GET /reports/feed-to-gain. then The response status is 200 and the returned report contains its filters, weightSelectionRule, and rows with the required lot, weight, ADG, feed, FCR, and feed-cost fields; the latest in-range weight and feeding events through that reading determine each row.\",\n    \"Given The API is running and project-demo content is available. when A client sends GET /project-demo. then The response status is 200 and the returned ProjectDemoResponse contains solutionSummary, architectureDiagram, demonstrationSteps, validationCoverage, challenges, productionReadiness, and goToMarket.\",\n    \"Given The requested datasetId is supported and the DemoLoadRequest is valid. when A client sends POST /demo-data/load. then The response status is 200 and the returned DemoLoadResponse contains datasetId, addedCount, alreadyPresentCount, failedCount, partial, and the three record-outcome lists.\",\n    \"Given A documented operation receives malformed input, a missing record, a conflict, invalid fields, or a service failure for which the contract documents an error response. when A client sends the request to that documented operation. then The response status is the operation's documented error status and the response body contains the ErrorResponse code and message fields, with details when present in the contract.\",\n    \"Given A lotId or batchId does not exist and the corresponding operation declares a 404 response. when A client sends the applicable forecast, assumption, preview, synchronization, or mapping request. then The response status is 404 and the response body contains the ErrorResponse code and message fields.\",\n    \"Given A nonexistent import batch is requested for preview. when A client sends POST /imports/preview with that batchId. then The response status is 404 and the response code field is not_found.\",\n    \"Given An inventory movement request references a nonexistent item. when A client sends POST /inventory/movements. then The response status is 404 and the response code field is not_found.\",\n    \"Given A horizon outside daily, weekly, monthly, quarterly, bi-annual, or annual is supplied. when A client sends GET /inventory/outlook. then The response status is 422 and the response body contains the ErrorResponse code and message fields.\",\n    \"Given A DemoLoadRequest body is invalid. when A client sends POST /demo-data/load. then The response status is 422 and the response body contains the ErrorResponse code and message fields.\",\n    \"Given The API project is built and running with its documentation page available. when A reviewer opens the available browser pages. then No product-facing feedlot screen is displayed and the available Swagger page is API documentation.\",\n    \"Given A feeding activity has been recorded and consumed ingredients are tracked in inventory. when A client reads GET /inventory/items after that feeding activity. then The response contains reduced stock for each consumed ingredient and the activity response's feedCost and lotConsumption values are available for the recorded event.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Feedlot API shall store persistent contract data in the PostgreSQL database configured by the existing App connection string and make saved records available after an application restart.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A PostgreSQL database configured using ConnectionStrings:App initially contains no application records. when A client creates, changes, or deletes persistent data using contract operations, the API process is restarted, and the corresponding list or detail operation is called again. then The response status is successful for the documented operation, each persisted row is returned with the saved field values, and a deleted row is absent from the response.\",\n    \"Given The application starts with a valid App PostgreSQL connection string. when The application initializes its database schema. then A database inspection finds row-capable persistent tables for the entities and relationships required by contract operations.\",\n    \"Given The App PostgreSQL database contains an inventory item used by a ration. when A client creates a ration referencing that item, the API restarts against the same database, and a client calls GET /rations. then The response contains the created ration record after restart.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When Seed:Demo is true, the Feedlot API shall populate each persistent contract entity table with believable sample rows based on contracts/openapi.yaml examples, so collection operations have sample data.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A fresh PostgreSQL database is configured and Seed:Demo is true. when The application starts and the contract collection operations are called. then Each persistent contract entity table contains at least three sample rows and each corresponding response list contains seeded records.\",\n    \"Given Seed:Demo is true and example records are available through the API. when A client reads the relevant import, lot, pen, inventory, and ration collections. then The response contains sample values modeled on contract examples, including spring-po-2026, PO-8041-L1, Lot 24-A, Pen 01, Yellow corn, and Grower 1.\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When Seed:Demo is false or absent, the Feedlot API shall operate without inserting demo rows or requiring demo data.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given PostgreSQL is empty and Seed:Demo is false or absent. when The application starts and contract API tests create prerequisite records through their own requests. then The database contains zero rows inserted by demo seeding and each response status and returned value in the tests is supported by test-created records.\",\n    \"Given The API is configured with Seed:Demo=false and an empty test database. when The application starts and a contract collection endpoint is called. then The response status is 200 and the returned list is empty without requiring demo rows.\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  \"All declared HTTP operations, request and response schemas, parameters, and status codes conform to the locked OpenAPI contract.\",\n  \"The deployed API contract must match the locked OpenAPI contract for all exposed operations, including paths, methods, parameters, JSON request and response schemas, and documented status codes.\",\n  \"The API implementation conforms to every operation in the locked OpenAPI contract.\",\n  \"Persistent application data must remain available through the configured PostgreSQL database across API restarts.\"\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\nRestate the change."}